  "notes": "An ichidan ({一段|いちだん}) verb. Also written without kanji as はげる. The kanji {禿|は}げ can be sensitive as a noun referring to a bald person — use with care in conversation.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {頭|あたま}が{禿|は}げる: to go bald\n- ペンキが{禿|は}げる: paint peels off\n- {山|やま}が{禿|は}げる: a mountain becomes bare\n- {禿|は}げ{上|あ}がる: to go completely bald (intensive)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {禿|は}げ: bald; bald person (noun) — can be considered rude\n- {薄毛|うすげ}: thinning hair — a more polite, euphemistic term\n- {脱毛|だつもう}: hair loss; hair removal — clinical/medical term\n- {剥|は}がれる: to peel off, come off — used for labels, stickers, surfaces",
